WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
I’ve always enjoyed the MCU, but I think Ant-Man&nbsp;
Quantumania is the straw to break marvel’s back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.460
Phase 4 was definitely rocky with movies like&nbsp;
Eternals, Black Widow, Thor: Love and Thunder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:16.500
and Doctor Strange, but at least those movies&nbsp;
were all relatively self-contained and were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.060
set with the tasks of telling an in-between&nbsp;
story from the infinity saga to the multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.960
saga. Marvel was starting to tear under the&nbsp;
sheer quantity they were outputting during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.400
phase 4 and now that Ant-Man Quantumania&nbsp;
was supposed to be the front runner that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.380
rocks everyone leading into phase 5 and it&nbsp;
being disappointing is upsetting. Initially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.100
I wasn’t going to do this review, but&nbsp;
I got a little fired up on Letterboxd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.880
so I’ll structure this video in a similar&nbsp;
way and won’t make it overly long.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:47.880
First, let’s go into the writing. Now I’m going&nbsp;
to be honest with you guys, I think this is one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:53.400
of the worst MCU scripts that has been put to the&nbsp;
screen so far. Which sucks because I had hope for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.260
Jeff Loveness. Given that he wrote some great&nbsp;
episodes for Rick and Morty. The usual marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.420
inclusion of humor rarely works once again and&nbsp;
detracts from the big dramatic requirement the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.580
movie needs given the mass stakes. One main reason&nbsp;
it doesn't work here in comparison to other marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:14.280
movies is because some scenes are solely based on&nbsp;
comedy like the Glup Shitto hole scene that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:20.040
just odd. Instead of the humor being reserved for&nbsp;
fast quips it takes a focus a lot of the time and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:25.200
it hurts entire scenes. Since this isn’t a quick&nbsp;
small-stakes adventure like the first two ant-man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.020
movies, I think this big blend of humor doesn’t&nbsp;
mix as well. Because quipping is fine every now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.940
and then, but scenes that should have more of a&nbsp;
dramatic focus don’t because of the humor. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.800
dialogue also feels really lazy like just throwing&nbsp;
quantum in front of things like the prior movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.500
Michael Douglas saying ANTS in every other&nbsp;
sentence which only made me think of this promo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.440
and no real sense of wit in any moment. The&nbsp;
movie was never able to get me to care about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:06.480
the character’s talking to each other and a major&nbsp;
aspect that relies on this was Cassie and Scott’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.400
relationship. It feels really tacked on for this&nbsp;
movie and the creators don’t do enough to make you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.660
care about their relationship. Considering that&nbsp;
the crux of the movie depends on their strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.940
bond, some dramatic beats fall short because&nbsp;
of this lack of connection between them. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.200
a lot of the sci-fi elements are overly&nbsp;
goofy like the controls for an alien ship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.360
having condom joysticks. The writing feels&nbsp;
like whatever random wacky shit the writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:35.700
wants to throw on screen instead of having any&nbsp;
semblance of coherency. I just constantly felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.080
detached from this world because it flat doesn’t&nbsp;
make sense when the writer makes no attempt at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:46.020
breathing logic into this world. Now having&nbsp;
wacky sci-fi concepts is fine, but when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.880
unload dozens of random elements in every scene&nbsp;
that aren’t complimentary, then it starts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.980
feel like an AI is generating the world for you.&nbsp;
Then the plot is not original enough and for how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.540
much time it galavants around pretending to be&nbsp;
Star Wars and you wish it was a movie primarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:06.060
about Kang. Because when he's around the movie&nbsp;
quickly becomes significantly better. That's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.520
only reason why I'd give this movie a 2/5. Once&nbsp;
he’s on-screen the tempo for Quantumania changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:17.460
instantly and all humor evaporates. The disparity&nbsp;
in quality between the wacky opening hour and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.560
Kang scenes are so massive to the point that if&nbsp;
you just isolated Kang’s scenes then this movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:28.500
becomes a 4/5. That’s why I think this movie has&nbsp;
such a big divide between critics and fans. Fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:33.300
will primarily focus on how awesome Kang is while&nbsp;
overlooking the faults the movie undoubtedly has.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.740
Which you should just be here for Kang at the&nbsp;
end of the day, so if you enjoyed the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:43.560
more than other people then that’s fine. But as an&nbsp;
overall package, this movie is extremely rough. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.700
can’t really go into detail about all the unique&nbsp;
writing issues because the movie isn’t out yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:52.560
but for once I think an MCU movie has enough&nbsp;
problems with the script to make a devoid of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.600
logic video. Normally there are some contrivances&nbsp;
and bad writing choices tied to Marvel movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.040
but I think Quantumania crosses the line and&nbsp;
there’s just so much wrong with the script.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:07.200
Going into the visual side of things, this has the&nbsp;
same issue as Thor: Love and Thunder where most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.180
of the set is just the ground and everything&nbsp;
else is CGI. While simultaneously trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:17.460
increase the scale the creators also strip away&nbsp;
the authenticity because everything feels fake.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:21.960
It's hard to get immersed when the actors can&nbsp;
barely interact with their surroundings and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:26.460
also leads to the most bland cinematography.&nbsp;
Because how can the cinematographer really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:31.320
get good footage when there’s almost nothing&nbsp;
practical on set. It basically just comes down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:36.780
to the pre-vis team to deliver iconic images that&nbsp;
are primarily driven by CGI. This reminds me of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.860
Star Wars again because for how much practical&nbsp;
elements there are within that film series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.600
it really makes that world feel real and&nbsp;
grounded. While Quantumania feels like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.700
it's on the opposite end of that spectrum. Then&nbsp;
the VFX isn't as bad as everyone loves to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:55.740
although I did spot a couple errors, but it has&nbsp;
some weird design choices and it's overloaded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:01.020
in every single frame making each shot feel&nbsp;
overwhelming. One of the weird design choices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:05.820
was Modok. I know he's supposed to look weird but&nbsp;
they shouldn't have scaled up his face by 400%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:11.220
and called it a day. Looking at his comic version&nbsp;
in comparison to the movie version is hilarious.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:16.140
For the acting and characters, the only person&nbsp;
here who gives a good performance is Jonathan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:21.360
Majors. He deserves a lot more for hard-carrying&nbsp;
this movie. Everyone else though has their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.400
distinct issue that hinders them. Paul Rudd to me&nbsp;
can't carry this big dramatic baggage because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:31.860
how much comedic lines he has to keep rattling off&nbsp;
in every scene. Again tying back to Thor needing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:36.960
to be dramatic but having a hard time fulfilling&nbsp;
that. Some of his moments with Kang do resonate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.740
really well because the humor disappears and&nbsp;
that’s the tone the movie should of had more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:45.540
of. Although that aspect of the movie would have&nbsp;
been better if the father and daughter bond was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:51.180
stronger. For Kathryn Newton, she was never able&nbsp;
to excel because of how generic Cassie Lang is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:56.160
She feels like a cookie-cutter character and her&nbsp;
only motivation in life is to do good and help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:01.440
people. So yeah, there’s not much there for her to&nbsp;
be that interesting and the movie quickly throws&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.780
us into the quantum realm so her introduction is&nbsp;
very brief. Then for Hope Van Dyne, she felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:11.760
a background character in the movie. She doesn’t&nbsp;
really lead any scene for dialogue and she just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.620
feels like she’s along for the ride. I’m surprised&nbsp;
the movie is called Ant-Man and the Wasp:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:22.080
Quantumania because of how little she has to do&nbsp;
in the plot. For Hank Pym, I genuinely believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.940
Michael Douglas regrets joining the MCU. It feels&nbsp;
like he isn’t trying anymore in some scenes which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:31.500
probably also has to do with the script and&nbsp;
making him say ants all the time, but he just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:36.180
seems bored. Like there are a few moments where&nbsp;
the characters are in a big plain of CGI vomit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:40.680
and Michael Douglas is just like yeah man, I&nbsp;
just don’t care about what’s happening right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:45.240
now. Then Michelle Pfeiffer is supposed to be&nbsp;
intriguing but since the script is so contrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:49.680
she's not allowed to tell anyone the crucial&nbsp;
information she holds until later in the movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.820
Like if she actually opened her mouth in the&nbsp;
beginning then none of this would have happened.

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:58.380
Ant-Man Quantumania really makes you wish we&nbsp;
could go back to the time of Captain America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:03.900
Winter Soldier because there the scripts felt so&nbsp;
much better. They weren't perfect by any means but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.040
at least they weren't a jumbled mess and told&nbsp;
a more riveting narrative. I don't know if I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:12.600
slowly changing and not liking the MCU anymore&nbsp;
because the people next to me loved it and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:17.640
theater was laughing hysterically at every joke.&nbsp;
To quote the people next to me: "That was fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:23.580
bro. It was fucking amazing." So yeah, everyone&nbsp;
has their own tastes and I’m falling on the side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:27.720
of the crowd who didn’t like the movie. There&nbsp;
are some other massive issues I have with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:33.000
movie regarding spoilers, but if you’ve seen it&nbsp;
then you know. Humpty Dumpty was done dirty. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.660
thank you for watching and let me know what&nbsp;
you guys thought about Ant-Man Quantumania.

